{"kind":"artifact","text":"The MCP projection notes at bff7dd1170bb679b6a8fd98231c5a5c8948f3729 on request/mcp-projection-notes. A state, ratify or supersede result now carries a `projected` object saying how the fold read the act: its ruling when that is not plain effect, citations naming no event in this workroom, a target naming none, and whether a report became a review a merge could act on. Existence is answered from projection.Decisions, which holds one row per durable record, so a citation naming a ratify or a supersede resolves rather than being reported as fabricated. A report that set body.verdict and was then ruled ineffective is told the verdict it submitted and the fold's reason, never that it omitted a field it did set. When the post-append snapshot cannot be read, every verb receives an explicit projected-unavailable diagnostic instead of a result indistinguishable from one where the fold found nothing. This replaces the candidate at 5fa6ba08, which stood at a branch name rather than a path any reader would cite.","body":{"commit":"bff7dd1170bb679b6a8fd98231c5a5c8948f3729","path":"cmd/gitseq-mcp"}}